  "headline_finding": "Regular-to-chaotic transfer (RC) works well (0/9 diverged, spike counts within 10% on 3/3 tests). Chaotic-to-regular transfer (CR) works ONLY when the test current falls inside or near the narrow confirmed-chaotic training span (2.98-3.40): interpolation cases (I=3.29, I=3.44) succeed, far-extrapolation (I=1.797) fails completely (wrong attractor). This is explained by training-span geometry, not an inherent asymmetry between chaos and regularity: the regular model trains across a much wider current span (1.42-3.80) which brackets nearly every chaotic test current, while the chaotic model only ever sees a narrow 0.41-wide band, making extrapolation far more likely when testing it on regular data.",
